# Post-Feature Selection Checkpoint

## Required Context
After selecting a feature, verify the following context elements:

1. Selected Feature Information
   - Feature name is clearly identified
   - Feature status in core-mechanics.mdc is updated to [in-progress]
   - Feature implementation file exists or has been created
   - Sub-features are identified and prioritized

2. Context Updates
   - active-working-feature-context.mdc is updated with the new feature
   - Previous feature is properly recorded in the history section
   - Current phase is accurately set to "Planning" or "Test Writing"

## Verification Steps
- [ ] Confirm the selected feature's status is now [in-progress] in core-mechanics.mdc
- [ ] Verify the implementation file exists with the correct structure
- [ ] Check that sub-features are identified with clear requirements
- [ ] Ensure active-working-feature-context.mdc reflects the new feature
- [ ] Validate that file paths and references are correct and accessible

## Context Synchronization
If any inconsistencies are detected:
1. Update core-mechanics.mdc to reflect the current feature as [in-progress]
2. Create or update the implementation file for the selected feature
3. Ensure active-working-feature-context.mdc is fully synchronized
4. Document the synchronization process and any changes made

## Expected Output
After completing this checkpoint, you should have:
- Selected feature clearly marked as [in-progress] in all relevant files
- Implementation file ready for development
- Active working context fully updated with the new feature information
- Clear understanding of the next steps in the implementation process 